  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content.html#dom-media-currentsrc\n\nThe `currentSrc` attribute is updated in the resource selection algorithm, but when a resource doesn't work out, it's not reset back to the empty string, like in this example:\n\n``` JavaScript\nvar v = document.createElement('video');\nv.src = 'data:,';\nv.onerror = function() {\n  console.log(v.networkState);\n  console.log(v.currentSrc)\n};\n```\n\nAt least Blink and Gecko end up with `NETWORK_NO_SOURCE` and yet `currentSrc` is 'data:,'.\n\nThis is unlikely to matter much, but is strange. I came to think of it in https://github.com/w3c/mediacapture-fromelement/issues/37\n",
